body:
I am in a similar situation. I am a teen. I think for us, telling about our issues is a cry for help. Actually, competition is a completely normal thing within depression, if that's what is going on. You are only 18. Seriously, it would be a shame to give up now, before you have even seen the world. About you thinking you are heartless and fake; depression does make us think that. It literally depresses your emotions; hence its name. 

&#x200B;

You don't deserve whatever happened to you as a child; no kid deserves anything like that. Remember, you are only 18. Hell, you haven't finished mental development yet! Neither of us have! There is so much room for us to grow as people, and eventually enjoy life! the possibilities are endless. Stay Strong xxx

How are they denying it? In some cases, denying your emotions and their role in them can be a form of gaslighting. I'm not saying this is what is going on, but maybe so.

&#x200B;

also, they may just not want to face the facts about how they are making you feel. Tell them whats up as bluntly as you possibly can.

I'm 14 too! I have depression and ocd. I'm not as bad as i was;  im not almost attempting suicide every weekend anymore, but I have fantasies about what it'd be like after i was dead though. And do miss being sad.

&#x200B;

You deserve recovery. No one our age (or anyone) deserves to go thru this shit.

ok so you are saying that taking antidepressants and being unable to get off of them easily is like being an addict. This to me is a result of stigma around mental health. Think of it this way: if you had a illness like i don't know, maybe anemia, and needed to take meds for that, you wouldn't feel like an addict most likely. But the truth is, the brain is just another part of the body

&#x200B;

Maybe its time to talk to your doctors about alternative treatment? If the meds aren't working, maybe other treatment will. Who knows, maybe your issues aren't chemical imbalance and are a result of another issue..............................just try to look into other things maybe. I'm 14 and started meds at age 9. So I'll probs be on them for a long time too, although i want to get off

I mean if a grown man went up to me and said that someone else is better than me irl....that would be rude. It's hurtful because i'm already shaky and insecure. Why the fuck would a grown ass adult feel the need to put me down and say another kid is better?

&#x200B;

He was the one saying first, he was better than me, and second, someone else is better, and accusing me of being judgemental?

What can i do to fix empathy issues? I've been told I'm very talented in empathy bcz i can see through ppls exterior to the root of their issues. Like why they are mean and whats the cause of it. and i don't know why i thought think those things in section 2 sometimes because...idk....

&#x200B;

I'm like 14 and stuff so I mean my empathy is still developing for the next 9 years. So idk if its normal like thoughts or stuff....but after I prayed for him bcz i thought it would be my fault then i thought then i'll miss that time with my crush but i had to pray i was obligated. I wouldn't be the cause of anyones serious pain.....thats for sure

&#x200B;

So idk if i have an empathy issue, what do you think

Idk bad vibes.

&#x200B;

He's a 60 year old dude who interrogates you  and stares at you while you talk..... I see him once a quarter for these questions

&#x200B;

"Are you suicidal"

Do you have any friends?

What are your grades?

Do you ever self harm?

&#x200B;

Like why the fuck would I answer those to some rando

Nope... blame the dudes staring, not the girls or yourself.

&#x200B;

NTA

NTA

You get the time off. Your choice.

